1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[theme song playing]

2
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
[roars]

3
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Strange beasts

4
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
and monsters.

5
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Vast riches.

6
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Hidden treasures.

7
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Evil haunts.

8
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Uncharted frontiers.

9
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,000
The mysterious unknown.

10
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

11
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
are called...

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Hunters.

13
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,000
DEPARTURE x AND x FRIENDS

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
WHALE ISLAND

15
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
[cawing]

16
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
[man 1] Is Gon still angling for
the Master of the Swamp?

17
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Uh, yes.

18
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
He's been at it non-stop
for a whole week now.

19
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,000
[man 2] So I gotta know...

20
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Did you really promise he could take
the Hunter Exam if he caught the thing?

21
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
[man 1]
He's a fool.

22
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Five adults working together
couldn't real that monster in.

23
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
So what chance does
a little kid have, huh?

24
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Sounds to me like Mito doesn't really
want him to take the Hunter Exam at all.

25
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
[man 1] Maybe so,
but wasn't Gon's old man his age

26
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
when he caught the Master of the Swamp?

27
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[man 2 laughs]
He doesn't stand a chance.

28
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
[gasps]

29
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Yeah!

30
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Ah, yes!
Here he comes.

31
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
[straining]

32
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
[cries out]

33
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
[yells]

34
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
[yelling]

35
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
[crying out]

36
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
[man 1]
Look at the size of it!

37
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
That's the Master of the Swamp?

38
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
[man 2]
Wow, it's been 20 years.

39
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
[man 1] Yeah, it was Gon's dad
who caught him last time, right?

40
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
[man 2]
Like father, like son.

41
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Gon really did it.
He actually caught the Master.

42
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Mito, over here!

43
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
[groans]

44
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Aunt Mito, look!
I caught him just like I said I would.

45
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
That means I can finally take
the Hunter Exam.

46
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Right?

47
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
I'll do my best.

48
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
I'm going to be a Hunter,
just you wait and see.

49
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
[great-grandmother]
It must be in his blood.

50
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Ging was only 12 years old
when he caught the Master

51
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
and no one has been able
to land him since.

52
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:58,000
And now his son has accomplished
the very same feat at the same age.

53
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:05,000
I don't have to tell you that his eyes
sparkle the same way as his father's.

54
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,000
It won't be long now
before we have to let him go.

55
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
-[Mito] Are you sure about this?
-[Gon] Yeah.

56
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:23,000
[Mito] When you were just a baby
your father abandoned you to be a Hunter.

57
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
You know that, don't you?

58
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,000
I do.

59
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
He chose being a Hunter
over his own son.

60
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
-[Gon] Yeah, isn't that amazing?
-[Mito] Huh?

61
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:37,000
It must be an awesome job
if it was worth leaving his kid.

62
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Don't you think?

63
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
But being a Hunter is a dangerous job.

64
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
You could die at any time
for any number of ridiculous reasons.

65
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
-[Mito] Don't you understand?
-[Gon sighs]

66
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:48,000
No, I don't.

67
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,000
But I want to understand.

68
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
I want to find out why it was so important
to my dad.

69
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
That's why I've got to do it.

70
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
[sighs]

71
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Just as I thought.
You're just like Ging.

72
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
I promise you. I'll pass the exam.

73
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
The next time you see me
I will be a Hunter.

74
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Instead, promise you'll come home safe.

75
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Think you can do that for me?

76
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Yep, I sure can.

77
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,000
[both]
Pinky swear, so if I lie

78
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:42,000
stick a thousand needles
in my eye.

79
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
And seal it with a...

80
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,000
-[Mito] kiss.
-[Gon] kiss...

81
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:54,000
[Gon draws out the word]

82
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
[laughs]

83
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Huh?
[Gon cries out]

84
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Gon.

85
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Aunt Mito, thank you.

86
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
[seagull cawing]

87
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
[everyone] Goodbye!

88
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
[man] Good luck, Gon!

89
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Get out there and knock 'em dead,
do you hear me?

90
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
We believe in you, buddy.

91
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Thanks, everybody. I'm going to be
the best Hunter in the world.

92
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,000
And as soon as I make that happen,
I'll be back.

93
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,000
I'll see you all again!

94
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
[man laughs]

95
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
The best Hunter in the world, huh?

96
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
The kid thinks this will be easy.

97
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
[man 2]
Every single year,

98
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,000
millions of the world's
most skilled applicants

99
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
apply for the Hunter Exam.

100
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
But only a handful make the cut.

101
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Be careful about saying stuff
you can't back up, kid.

102
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
[men laugh]

103
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
[man 1]
What are you doing, Katzo?

104
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
[man 2]
With the way things are going for you,

105
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
you're never going to make it as a sailor.

106
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
-[laughter]
-[Katzo yelps]

107
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,000
[laughter]

108
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
What's wrong?
Why are you bent over like that?

109
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
[captain]
Hey, slackers.

110
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Get back to work!

111
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
[men]
Aye, aye, sir.

112
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
[Katzo groans]

113
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
You!

114
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Got wax in your ears?
Get moving!

115
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Aye, aye, sir. Right away

116
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
[Gon] Wait!

117
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
[gasps]

118
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
Thanks a lot.

119
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
There's a storm coming.

120
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
[captain] Huh?

121
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
And how exactly do you know that?

122
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Sea cranes.
That's what all of them are saying.

123
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,000
What?

124
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Also...

125
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
[inhales deeply]

126
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
There's a really big one
heading right for us.

127
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
-[groans]
-[Gon] It's true.

128
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
I can tell by the way it smells.

129
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
[captain] This boy...

130
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Those eyes.

131
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Could he be...

132
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[thunder clapping]

133
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,000
[ocean rumbling loudly]

134
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
[everyone screaming]

135
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Captain!

136
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
The mast won't hold out for much longer.

137
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
We should lower the sails.

138
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Don't be stupid.

139
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:19,000
We can't quit when the fun is
just about to start.

140
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[chuckles]

141
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Here we go!

142
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Now, take her hard to port.

143
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
[yelling] Let's fly!

144
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:49,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

145
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:53,000
GON

146
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
[men groaning]

147
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Ahh! I've faced bigger waves than that
and lived.

148
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Hey, take over the helm.

149
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Aye, aye, sir.

150
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,000
[gagging]

151
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Damned if this ain't the most
worthless crew I've seen in years.

152
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
[men groaning]

153
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Not a one of them has got
his sea legs. Pathetic.

154
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
And they think they can pass
the Hunter Exam?

155
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
They're good for a laugh,
that's for sure.

156
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
-[Gon] Here, try these herbs.
-Hm?

157
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Chew them up real good
and you'll feel better.

158
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[struggling to speak]
Water...

159
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
[Gon] Sit tight, it's on its way.

160
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Huh, that boy again.

161
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
[crunching]

162
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,000
[captain] Hm.

163
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
[crackling, chewing]

164
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,000
[groaning]

165
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
That's what I call a sour apple.

166
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
[captain] Huh, I see.

167
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Seems there's a few
with some iron in them, after all.

168
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
-Coming through.
-[captain grumbles]

169
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
Here, I got you water.

170
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Thank you.

171
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
[Gon] There, drink up.

172
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
[gulping water]

173
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
[Katzo sighs]

174
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
[grumbles]

175
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
[chuckles]

176
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Hm.

177
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Hm?

178
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
You're the best.
Thanks for your help, Mr. Katzo.

179
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
[ocean rumbling loudly]

180
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
[captain] Right, then. Go down the line
and tell me all your names.

181
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
My name's Gon.

182
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,000
I am called Kurapika.

183
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
The name is Leorio.

184
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Good, good. Now why do you boys want
to become Hunters?

185
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:43,000
Whoa! You're not an examiner,
so what's with the third degree?

186
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Just answer the question, dummy.

187
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,000
I will. Because my dad is a Hunter.

188
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Hm?

189
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:54,000
[Gon] Being a hunter was the most
important thing in the world to my dad.

190
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,000
And I want to know why.

191
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,000
That's why I left Whale Island.

192
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Whale Island?

193
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
So it is him.
This is Ging's son.

194
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
It looks like the day has come at last.

195
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
[Leorio] Hey, kid.

196
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
You don't have to tell
that old guy nothin'.

197
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
But he asked why I'm here.
It's not a secret.

198
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Look, get with the program.
It's us versus him.

199
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
And I'm not telling him
why I'm here.

200
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
[Kurapika] I'm afraid I agree with Leorio.

201
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Huh?

202
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,000
That's Mr. Leorio to you, you brat.

203
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Show a little respect for your elders.

204
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,000
But why not dodge the question

205
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
by simply offering the man
a plausible lie?

206
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Hey! Are you even listening to me?

207
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,000
However, it is quite shameful
to rely upon deceit.

208
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,000
As for me,

209
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
I cannot reveal my reasons here.

210
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
I have my share of secrets.

211
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Deep secrets, which I do not intend
to expose at this time.

212
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
That is why
I will not answer your question.

213
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Hey, I was talking to you, punk.

214
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[captain] So, both of you flat out refuse
to answer my question.

215
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Hey, Katzo.

216
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Yes, what is it, Captain?

217
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Get a hold of the Exam Committee for me.

218
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Let them know we've got two more dropouts.

219
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
[both gasp]

220
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Wait, what do you mean?

221
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Still haven't figured it out, huh?

222
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
You see,
the Hunter Exam has already started.

223
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,000
[both] It has?

224
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:22,000
[captain] There are as many
Hunter wannabes in this world

225
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
as there are stars in the sky.

226
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
And the examiners, well...

227
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:30,000
The fact is, they don't have the time
nor the resources to go through them all.

228
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,000
That's where people like me come in
to pick up the slack.

229
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Screen all of the applicants
and trim the fat.

230
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
I've already notified the committee

231
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,000
about the rest of the lot.
Not a one of them made the cut.

232
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,000
-[Leorio] What?
-[Kurapika] Huh?

233
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
[captain] That was just a little storm
and look how they handled it.

234
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
They'd never survive
the later stages of the exam.

235
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,000
In other words,

236
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:55,000
the only way you three are moving on
to the next portion of the Exam

237
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
is if I give you the go-ahead.

238
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:02,000
So, I'll ask you again.
And think carefully before you answer.

239
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,000
You catch all that?

240
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Hm?

241
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
[Leorio]
You could have told us that sooner.

242
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
I am the sole survivor
of the Kurta Clan.

243
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Four years ago,

244
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:21,000
my entire clan was annihilated
by a band of criminals.

245
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
That is why I want to become a Hunter.

246
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
To capture the Phantom Troupe.

247
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Sounds like you want to be
a Black List Hunter.

248
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
And the Phantom Troupe is
a Class-A bounty.

249
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
Even the most seasoned Hunters
can't touch them.

250
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
You know it's a suicide mission, right?

251
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Death is not among my fears.

252
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:48,000
But there is one thing I do fear,
and one thing alone.

253
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
That time will quiet the rage in my heart.

254
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
So, in other words,
you're out for revenge.

255
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,000
But you don't really need to become
a Hunter

256
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
just so you can settle an old score,
do you?

257
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:04,000
That is the stupidest question
I have ever heard, Leorio.

258
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
That's "Mr. Leorio."

259
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
There are places only Hunters can go,

260
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
intel only they can access,

261
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
and actions only they can take.

262
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,000
There are more reasons

263
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
but those are the only three
that you have a chance of comprehending.

264
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
-[screaming]
-[Gon] Hey!

265
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Why do you want to become a Hunter,
Mr. Leorio?

266
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Who, me?

267
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Well, it's pretty simple, really.

268
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,000
-For the money.
-Huh?

269
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,000
[loudly] Money can buy everything
you've ever wanted.

270
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
A big mansion.

271
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
A cool car.

272
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,000
And top-shelf booze.
[chuckles]

273
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:44,000
If only you could buy class as well,
Leorio.

274
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
That was strike three.

275
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Step outside.

276
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Time to finish off the
filthy Kurta bloodline once and for all.

277
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Take that back, Leorio!

278
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,000
I said, take it back.

279
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,000
It's "Mr. Leorio."

280
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
[captain]
Hey, where do you boys think you're going?

281
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,000
I'm not finished with you yet.

282
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,000
[Gon] Let them go.

283
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
They're fine.
It's like Aunt Mito told me once,

284
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:29,000
You can never understand a person unless
you can understand what makes them angry.

285
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,000
It's how you get to know someone.

286
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:37,000
So whatever they're feeling so upset about
is really important to them.

287
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:41,000
It's up to them now.
Nothing we can do but stay out of the way.

288
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,000
[crewman] Captain!

289
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Look. Over there.

290
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
[grunts]

291
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,000
[thunder claps]

292
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:58,000
If we get caught up in that waterspout,
the ship is going to sink for sure.

293
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
Get the sails lowered. Now!

294
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:01,000
-Right.
-Anything I can do?

295
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Yeah, follow me up on deck.

296
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:06,000
-Go with them. I'll take the helm.
-Aye!

297
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,000
All right, then, hard to starboard.

298
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
[sailor] Move it!

299
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:15,000
If we get caught in the waterspout
we're done for!

300
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:18,000
-[men clamoring]
-[ship creaking]

301
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[Gon straining]

302
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Take back what you said about my clan.

303
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,000
I will forgive you if you repent, Leorio.

304
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
You owe me an apology.

305
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
And I'm not telling you again.

306
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,000
I'm not repenting for anything,
hear me?

307
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,000
[softly] Very well.

308
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,000
[men crying out]

309
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
[Gon] Mr. Katzo!

310
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,000
[grunts]

311
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
[groaning]

312
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,000
[both] Damn!

313
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
Come on, let's get them back on deck!

314
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
[straining]

315
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,000
[Leorio] You idiot!

316
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:50,000
If it hadn't been for us,
you'd be shark bait.

317
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:53,000
You owe me big time, kid.
And don't you forget it.

318
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Honestly, how reckless can you be?

319
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
But it's fine, you caught me.

320
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
-Huh?
-Huh?

321
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:03,000
You both did.
You both caught me together.

322
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
I guess you might have a point.

323
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,000
[Katzo] Gon!

324
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,000
[Gon] Hey, Mr. Katzo.

325
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Thanks, Gon, you're incredible.

326
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
You saved my life back there.

327
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Yeah, well, I didn't do it all alone.

328
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Those two over there
helped rescue you, too.

329
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
[Katzo]
He's right. Thank you both.

330
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Please. No thanks necessary.

331
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
Yeah, no prob.

332
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
We're just glad to see
you made it okay.

333
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Me too.

334
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
In fact, I ought to get back to my post
right away.

335
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
[Leorio chuckles]
Hm?

336
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:42,000
[Kurapika chuckles]

337
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,000
What's so funny?

338
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
I'm embarrassed at my behavior.

339
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Pardon my rudeness, Mr. Leorio.

340
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,000
I wasn't expecting that.

341
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
Just forget it.

342
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:57,000
You can drop the Mister.
Leorio is fine.

343
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
I'm sorry, too.

344
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:05,000
And I take back everything
that I said to you before.

345
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,000
That was wrong of me.

346
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:09,000
[Kurapika] No, it's fine.

347
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:13,000
[captain laughs]

348
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:18,000
You three are growing on me.
So...

349
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
I'll make sure all three of you
get safely dropped off

350
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:26,000
at the port closest to the Exam site.
How does that sound? [chuckles]

351
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,000
You will?

352
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:29,000
[Kurapika]
But, what about your test?

353
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:35,000
It's like I said, I decide who goes on
to take the Exam.

354
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Congratulations!
You're all moving on.

355
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,000
[chuckles]

356
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,000
[sighs]

357
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:46,000
[loudly] All right! [chuckles]

358
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
[narrator]
And so, Gon finally began his journey

359
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,000
to do what his father did
before him.

360
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
To become a Hunter.

361
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
[theme song playing]

362
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Test x of x Tests."

363
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
Don't miss it!
